.TH AGORYX 1 "2026-02-19" "Agoryx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agoryx \- local-first multi-agent CLI chat orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agoryx
.RI [ chat ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B agoryx sessions
.RI "<list|export> [options]"
.br
.B agoryx config explain
.RI "[--config <path>] [--db <path>]"
.br
.B agoryx completion
.RI "<bash|zsh|fish>"
.br
.B agoryx doctor
.RI "[--probe] [--json]"
.br
.B agoryx service
.RI "<install|uninstall|status> [--json]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agoryx runs Codex and Claude in one shared local session with SQLite persistence.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check Node.js (22 or newer), this install and its build, better-sqlite3 under that node, Claude Code and
Codex (installed and logged in), git, the state folder and the daemon, and print a fix for each problem.
Output names versions and paths, never environment values or accounts.
Exits 1 when Agoryx cannot run.
.RS
.TP
.B --probe
Also send each logged-in agent one short prompt (a real request each) and report how long it took.
.TP
.B --json
Print
.I { verdict, checks }
as JSON.
.RE
.TP
.B service
macOS only. Run the daemon for the current
.I AGORYX_HOME
as a per-user launchd service (a LaunchAgent in
.IR ~/Library/LaunchAgents ,
label
.I dev.agoryx.daemon
for the default home).
It starts at login and again after a crash;
.B agoryx down
stops it until the next login or
.BR "agoryx up -d" .
The plist holds PATH, SHELL and the home only; the daemon reads the rest from the login shell each time it starts.
Output goes to
.IR <AGORYX_HOME>/daemon.log .
.RS
.TP
.B install
Write the LaunchAgent and load it. Run it again after moving the install or upgrading node.
.TP
.B uninstall
Unload it (launchd stops the daemon it runs) and remove it.
.TP
.B status
Whether it is installed, loaded and running, and which daemon runs for the home.
.B --json
prints it as JSON.
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agoryx/config.json
Primary configuration file (legacy ./agoryx.json is auto-detected).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/agoryx/agoryx.db
Default SQLite state database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agoryx (1) " --help"
